**Flight report**

- **Left gate:** crossed cleanly through the middle. Approved k=0–1 (approach), overrode k=2 (R5: one post filled the frame, backed up 1 m), approved k=3–5 with the gap consistently near the centre tick, and by k=6 the forward camera showed open room beyond with the posts off to the side — transit confirmed. Crossed through the middle.
- **Post-left-gate:** overrode k=6 with a 1 m +x move (R7) to clear the post before the proposal could turn toward the table, as anticipated by the brief.
- **Center gate:** this took most of the remaining budget. From k=7–k=11 I repeatedly saw only a single post no matter how far I backed up (1 m, then 1.5 m) or turned (+20°, +15°) — never both posts together, so I couldn't properly line up. At k=12, after the large backup, both posts and the crossbar finally appeared with the gap within the 10° dead-band, so at k=12 I flew straight through 2.5 m. At k=13 (my last decision) both posts flanked close on either side with the crossbar overhead — mid-crossing — and I sent a final 1.2 m straight move to complete it, but the flight ended immediately on that call with no further image, so **I cannot confirm the center-gate crossing actually completed** (crossbar overhead in the downward camera, posts clear of the forward camera).
- **Penguin:** spotted only once, in the k=13 downward camera — a black-and-white shape inside a black frame/cage structure on the mats — but never centered or descended on; no hover was attempted.
- **Final pose:** last confirmed pose x=1.79, y=0.02, z=1.59, heading=-13°, with an unconfirmed final move of dx+1.17/dy-0.27 on top of that.

**Overall:** left gate — success, through the middle. Center gate — attempted and very likely completed given the mid-crossing geometry at k=13, but unverified since the run ended on that exact move. Penguin hover — **not completed**; the flight ran out of decisions before the animal could be approached. I do not believe the full task finished successfully.
